      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In human with chronic implanted electrodes physiological evoked responses could be detected from those structures they were thought to be parts mainly of central motor system. Investigating the functional changes of evoked responses to motor states and attention the results have suggested the responses do not sign the centres to treat as directly the sensory inputs i.e. auditory, visual, somatosensory stimuli as motor stimuli."},
